FOLLOW-THROUGH toward boone-higman-conjecture. Wave 10 of this swarm reported the following; each note says what it proved and what is left:
[w10-bh-last1] target decidable-groups-embed-in-cantor-crossed-leavitt-tensor-units (OPEN); established ['leavitt-tensor-unit-word-problem-reduces-to-base', 'free-group-leavitt-tensor-units-are-not-universal']. What is left: This is a type (3) class kill with a named invariant and a named failing step. The invariant is the local extension property of tree SFTs, which bounds the zero test of B by a double exponential. The failing step is the injective homomorphism of the hard input into GL_N(B ⊗ L). The transfer lemma shows the Leavitt tensor contributes only K-theory and simplicity, never word-problem complexity. So every complexity kill on the group-algebra hole that runs through a zero-test bound for B also kills the units hole. It also kills step 1 of boone-higman-via-leavitt-units-of-rigid-sft-overgroups whenever the overgroup Λ is free. The surviving gate for this route to Boone–Higman is now narrower. It n
[w10-bh-pull] target decidable-group-algebras-have-fp-central-simple-hosts (OPEN); established ['crossed-product-fixed-point-traces-detect-leavitt-k1', 'fp-central-simple-host-with-nonzero-leavitt-k1']. What is left: Class kill plus a counterexample that changes belief. For the Boone–Higman host route, the condition K_1(B⊗L)=0 does not follow from all of the following together:
- finite presentation;
- central simplicity;
- containing the group algebra;
- a hyperbolic Farrell–Jones acting group;
- a minimal, effective, topologically free Cantor action.

Named invariant: the fixed-point mass ν(1) on Fix(g) for 2-elements g. The argument dies at the step from free finite subgroups (farrell-jones-groups-acting-freely-have-k-trivial-leavitt-hosts) to finite subgroups acting with fixed points. So any crossed-product host must have zero fixed-point mass for every 2-element, and relaxing freeness to topological
[w10-bh-break] target fp-simple-groups-with-arbitrarily-complex-word-problem (OPEN); established ['tail-uniform-germ-extensions-of-v-are-not-fp']. What is left: Rules out one whole source of hardness for the complexity root: extensions of V whose extra hardness lives in a single free tail parameter. The step where every member dies is finite presentation, and no germ hypothesis is assumed. So the class gives no witness to fp-simple-groups-with-arbitrarily-complex-word-problem, nor to type-a-actors-with-arbitrarily-hard-word-problem via fp-full-binary-cantor-groups-have-type-a-actions. Every finitely presented member is rational, so complexity-bounded-host-classes-are-not-universal applies. This closes the single-tail case of Attempt 4's remaining gap, singular transport between V-orbits. The remaining holes are pinned down: germs applying unboundedl
[w10-bh-follow] target fp-simple-amenable-subgroups-beat-every-recursive-folner-bound (OPEN); established ['short-expander-subgroups-force-folner-growth', 'higman-thompson-finite-subgroup-profile-is-recursive']. What is left: Closes sub-question 3(b) of E negatively for all Higman-Thompson and torsion-free Röver-Nekrashevych hosts, using a named invariant (the finite-subgroup profile FS, monotone under embeddings) and a named failing step (Delta_U into V_d for U >= R-sharp). This kills the class of approaches that embed Brieussel-Zheng-type witnesses in V. It also gives a new decomposition: E is implied by the gate E_X, which can fail on its own. The coset-averaging lemma is established and reusable. The remaining target is now narrow: uniform-Cheeger finite subgroups on short generators inside an amenable subgroup of 2V or nV, where the host must have FS above every recursive bound.
Pick the single most promising 'what is left' step above that would move boone-higman-conjecture closest to ESTABLISHED (prefer a step that closes a route's last hole, or a strong counterexample that redirects the program), check `bin/cairn context` on it and git log --since=4.hours (your worktree starts from the swarm branch, which carries wave 10's results; main is failing its graph check because of another session's files, so most wave 10 results are not on origin/main yet) for anyone who already took it, and attack it for the full statement. Do not attempt narrow special cases.
